From: damnbitimcrit <333091414+damnbitimcrit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Halo 3] Smooth cameras, HUD messages and animated shaders;
 more stats

- Cutscene cameras (scripted camera modes 2, 3 and 5) advance in whole
  ticks. Keep the camera of the last two ticks and draw their blend, one
  tick late like the objects, at the common tail of the scripted camera
  update (822928F8). Cuts (a new camera command, a different scene, shot or
  animation, or a big jump) are shown as is.
- A driver seat's third-person camera focus, and the following camera's
  collision start, are the vehicle's centre of mass from its physics body,
  which only changes in ticks while the vehicle is drawn blended. Move both
  points by the blend of the root object's node 0 (820A0820, 822959D4).
- HUD messages time their pop-in zoom and fades by age in whole ticks: add
  the tick fraction. Their scroll and one compounding fade step once per
  main loop pass: scale them by frame time. The medal animation's time in
  the draw gets the fraction too.
- The game time render_method animated parameters read, the tree sway
  timer and one pass's constant are whole ticks: add the fraction on the
  thread that draws (halo3_smooth_shader_time, on by default).
- Steps taken once per main loop pass (HUD fades, the cinematic HUD
  fade) are scaled for the original's 60 passes per second, not 30.
- Stats: blend drops by reason and object type, frames without a blend,
  whether player 0's vehicle is blended, camera blends and cuts, shader
  times smoothed, and the auto exposure readback (the scene brightness the
  game reads back from the GPU and the exposure it picks).
